# Python Web Application - Dockerized

A simple Python web application containerized using Docker. This project demonstrates how to build, run, and deploy a Python application using Docker on a local machine or an AWS EC2 instance.

---

## 📂 Project Structure

```text
python-app/
├── app.py
├── requirements.txt
├── Dockerfile
└── README.md
```

---

## 🚀 Prerequisites

Before running this project, ensure you have:

- Docker installed
- Git installed
- Ubuntu/Linux server (Optional: AWS EC2 Instance)

Verify installation:

```bash
docker --version
git --version
```

---

## 📥 Clone Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/<your-github-username>/<repository-name>.git
cd <repository-name>
```

Example:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/johndoe/python-app.git
cd python-app
```

---

## 🏗️ Build Docker Image

Build the Docker image from the Dockerfile:

```bash
docker build -t python-web-app .
```

Verify image creation:

```bash
docker images
```

Expected output:

```bash
REPOSITORY       TAG       IMAGE ID       CREATED
python-web-app   latest    xxxxxxxxxxxx   1 minute ago
```

---

## ▶️ Run Docker Container

Start the application:

```bash
docker run -d -p 8000:8000 --name python-app python-web-app
```

Verify the container is running:

```bash
docker ps
```

Expected output:

```bash
CONTAINER ID   IMAGE            STATUS
xxxxxxxxxxxx   python-web-app   Up 10 seconds
```

---

## 🌐 Access the Application

### Local Machine

Open:

```text
http://localhost:8000
```

### AWS EC2

Open:

```text
http://<EC2-PUBLIC-IP>:8000
```

Example:

```text
http://35.154.xx.xx:8000
```

> Make sure port **8000** is allowed in the EC2 Security Group.

---

## 📜 View Container Logs

```bash
docker logs python-app
```

Real-time logs:

```bash
docker logs -f python-app
```

---

## 🔍 Enter Running Container

```bash
docker exec -it python-app bash
```

---

## ⏹️ Stop Container

```bash
docker stop python-app
```

---

## ▶️ Start Existing Container

```bash
docker start python-app
```

---

## 🔄 Restart Container

```bash
docker restart python-app
```

---

## 🗑️ Remove Container

```bash
docker stop python-app
docker rm python-app
```

---

## 🗑️ Remove Docker Image

```bash
docker rmi python-web-app
```

---

## 🔧 Rebuild After Code Changes

Whenever application code changes:

```bash
docker stop python-app
docker rm python-app

docker build -t python-web-app .

docker run -d -p 8000:8000 --name python-app python-web-app
```

---

## 🚀 Deployment on AWS EC2

### 1. Connect to EC2

```bash
ssh -i key.pem ubuntu@<EC2-PUBLIC-IP>
```

### 2. Clone Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/<your-github-username>/<repository-name>.git
cd <repository-name>
```

### 3. Build Docker Image

```bash
docker build -t python-web-app .
```

### 4. Run Container

```bash
docker run -d -p 8000:8000 --name python-app python-web-app
```

### 5. Access Application

```text
http://<EC2-PUBLIC-IP>:8000
```

---

## 🔄 Update Application

When new code is pushed to GitHub:

```bash
git pull

docker stop python-app || true
docker rm python-app || true

docker build -t python-web-app .

docker run -d -p 8000:8000 --name python-app python-web-app
```

---

## 🐳 Push Image to Docker Hub

### Login

```bash
docker login
```

### Tag Image

```bash
docker tag python-web-app <dockerhub-username>/python-web-app:latest
```

### Push Image

```bash
docker push <dockerhub-username>/python-web-app:latest
```

Example:

```bash
docker tag python-web-app harshsaini/python-web-app:latest
docker push harshsaini/python-web-app:latest
```

### Pull Image Anywhere

```bash
docker pull <dockerhub-username>/python-web-app:latest
```

### Run Pulled Image

```bash
docker run -d -p 8000:8000 --name python-app <dockerhub-username>/python-web-app:latest
```

---

## 🛠️ Troubleshooting

### Application Not Accessible

Check container status:

```bash
docker ps
```

### View Logs

```bash
docker logs python-app
```

### Verify Port Mapping

```bash
docker ps
```

Expected:

```bash
0.0.0.0:8000->8000/tcp
```

### AWS Security Group

Allow:

| Type | Port | Source |
|--------|--------|--------|
| Custom TCP | 8000 | 0.0.0.0/0 |

